{* A block of text the user is meant to take away: shown in full, selectable, with a copy button.

	A textarea rather than an input because the things that end up here are long — an absolute
	path into a macOS bundle runs well past any sensible field width, and an input shows one
	field-width of it with no hint there is more. A textarea wraps, so the whole command is visible
	without scrolling it horizontally.

	readonly, not disabled: a disabled control cannot be selected or copied, which is the only
	thing this exists for. Its rows come from the caller, since only the caller knows how long
	the content runs.

	The button is wired by src/Assets/javascript/copy-field.js, which binds every instance on the
	page by data attribute — no id to keep unique, and no inline handler, which the app's CSP
	would refuse anyway (strict-dynamic makes the 'unsafe-inline' beside it ignored).
*}
{parameters
	string $value,
	string $label,
	string $copy,
	string $copied,
	int $rows = 2
}
<div class="ad-copy" data-copy-field>
	<textarea class="ad-copy-value" readonly rows="{$rows}" aria-label="{$label}"
		data-copy-value>{$value}</textarea>
	<button type="button" class="ad-copy-button" data-copy-button data-copied="{$copied}">{$copy}</button>
</div>
